# Knowledge map

Always read [`STATE.md`](STATE.md) first. This file is navigation, not an independent theorem source.

## Five-minute orientation

1. [`STATE.md`](STATE.md) — exact current theorem lifecycle/status.
2. [`problem/statement.md`](problem/statement.md) — Level I quantifiers.
3. Pick one route map:
   - [`targets/target-a/README.md`](targets/target-a/README.md)
   - [`targets/target-b/README.md`](targets/target-b/README.md)
   - [`targets/target-c/README.md`](targets/target-c/README.md)
4. Read only the canonical modules/reports named there.
5. Read the current route prompt from [`prompts/README.md`](prompts/README.md) last.

For research workflow also read [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) and [`RESEARCH_WORKFLOW.md`](RESEARCH_WORKFLOW.md).

## Current route summaries

### Target A

Canonical development runs through Section 177. The Section-167 source-labeled Menger endpoint and Section-174 full basis-closed shield penalty are historical. Section 175 reduces the locked branch to the interior-tube right-deficiency inequality `|O_iso| + sum_i max(0,|O_i|-|C_i|) >= j_* + |T_Z|`. Section 176 proves the zero-slack inner-source defect is at most `12d+9` and localizes every saturating source matching to contact-shield sectors outside an explicit boundary-order exceptional set. Target A remains open.

### Target B

The canonical endpoint remains the joint outer-shell stability inequality. The September 11 independent dense-grid / penetration / interpolation audit promotes DT1–DT4, TG1–TG3, PDG, PC1/PC3, MCP1, fixed-`lambda` MCP2, and GPI under their exact pure-disk/coherent-component hypotheses. These are canonical scoped tools, not a multi-grain globalization; the global transfer across several macroscopic coherent grains remains open.

### Target C

Start at [`targets/target-c/CURRENT.md`](targets/target-c/CURRENT.md), not chronological report search.

Current canonical state:

1. C-I is closed; C-II remains open.
2. Zero/additive response transfer is excluded in the promoted regime.
3. ZR/ZF is scoped to the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`: `ker Omega_V=span{1,Px|_V,Py|_V}`, mixed core rigidity rank `2v-3`, `e+h>=2v-2`, and `h>=delta>=ceil(D)`. Contact-isolated source points remain in the full configuration.
4. Sections 58–69 give full-source geometry, difference-body density/stability, nonmatching and attachment currency, all-topology population transport, punctured phase control, and a forced quadratic coherent physical grain in the quadratic-core branch.
5. Section 70 gives sharp Woodall-forest endpoint area/inradius and a linear family of distinct shallow inward contacts. Section 71 gives selected-extreme attachment separation/perimeter control with the genuine deficiency and pinned-nullity terms retained.
6. Section 72 is canonical only in the exact primitive all-loaded shell `m=0`, `d_H+s_Z=2`, `C=C_q`: `dim S=s_Z=2-d_H`, every full-H leaf diameter edge stays positive throughout `S`, and for `s_Z>0` at least `s_Z+1=3-d_H` nonleaf–nonleaf diameter edges occur. No facet-derived lower bound is asserted for `(d_H,s_Z)=(2,0)`.
7. Section 73 closes grid extraction in the quadratic-core branch even with holes: a Section-69 grain with `R` rhombi and `T=P/2` trains has complete internally noncrossing shores `>=c_PS R/T` and a complete distinct-phase subgrid with shores `>=(c_PS/2)R/T=Omega(D)`.
8. Section 74 collapses half of each linear phase-pure shore to inverse-diameter phase width: every retained complete-grid rhombus has angle `pi/3+O(1/D)`. The live obstruction is boundary-budget common-order/penetration or a direct diameter contradiction.
9. The full loaded diameter graph has the exact Woodall topology split and all selected diameter routes meet one common positive-contact bridge block.
10. The independently audited PR #188 and PR #182 scalar chains remain canonical. The pocket-degree numerical optimizer near `0.767...` remains exploratory.
11. PR #191's `0.995540...` theorem remains rejected because the inward pocket and exterior Reuleaux minor cap lie on opposite sides of the force-hull chord.
12. In the narrow primitive `d_H=1,s_Z=1` endpoint, P1 is excluded; S1 remains open under the reciprocal-square reduction; the finite `q=13` KKT/PSD object is a regression rather than a global-minimizer theorem.

### Target C dead-route checklist

Do not use older reports that require any of these rejected implications unless a new proof explicitly repairs them:

- incident diameter sequence `=>` Euler trail/path;
- FB4 force-bulk localization;
- incompatible-cut pentagon objection to C53;
- RSR disk-equality uniqueness;
- Eppstein near-equality `=>` near quadrangulation;
- five-host measure saturation `=>` all five hosts populated;
- inward OP pocket contained in the exterior Reuleaux minor cap;
- dropping contact-isolated source points;
- extending the Section-57 affine-kernel theorem to contact-isolated source coordinates.

